terse removes words. it does not remove the subject.

"built." "answered yes, twice over." "reachable, and better than
expected:" — each saves three words and costs the reader the thing the
sentence is about.

the test: read the line with nothing before it. if you cannot say what
it is about, the subject was not noise.

`general/terse:/delete the line/` is the cut. this is the floor under
it, and `general/human:/terse serves comprehension/` is why there is one.
